  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: out-of-bounds write in pcre2_dfa_match() because\n     more_workspace() reused a cached recursive-DFA workspace block without\n     checking it was large enough for the request, so a pattern using nested\n     assertions followed by recursion under a small heap limit could overflow\n     the heap allocation (PCRE2 before 10.48)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-86145.patch: reject a cached next block smaller\n       than the requested size, and clamp a newly allocated block to the\n       remaining heap allowance without overflowing the size computation, in\n       more_workspace() in src/pcre2_dfa_match.c\n     - CVE-2026-86145",
